---
layout: base.njk
title: Find Your People on the Mountain
description: Plan your ski day with mountain weather, snow forecasts and powder alerts. Find riding partners, explore trail maps and track your runs with SkiBuds. Coming soon.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
preloadHero: true
pageScripts:
  - waitlist-form.js
  - resort-sections.js
---

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="hero">
  {% image "/images/WhistlerPeakView.jpg", "Skiers on Whistler mountain", "100vw", "hero__bg", "eager", "high", [640, 1080, 1920] %}
  <div class="shell">
    {% image "logo.png", "SkiBuds logo", "108px", "hero__logo rise", "eager", "high" %}
    <h1 class="rise rise--2">Find your people on the mountain</h1>
    <p class="lede rise rise--3">
      Find the snow. Find your crew. Make a day of it. Mountain weather, riding partners,
      trail maps, and run tracking &mdash; together in SkiBuds.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__actions rise rise--3">
      <a href="/weather/" class="btn" data-track-cta="hero-weather">Explore mountain weather &rarr;</a>
      <a href="#about" class="hero__link">See what&rsquo;s in the app</a>
    </div>

    <p class="hero__availability rise rise--3">In the works for iOS &amp; Android <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> {{ site.app.launchYear }}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Weather -->
<section class="band weather-spotlight" id="weather" aria-labelledby="weather-heading">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="feature-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Mountain weather, at the center of your day</p>
        <h2 id="weather-heading">The right mountain.<br>The right window.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">
        An overnight storm. A windy summit. A clear afternoon. SkiBuds brings snow,
        temperature, wind, and visibility into the same picture so you can decide
        where to ride and when to get there.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="forecast-overview" aria-label="Weather features in the upcoming app">
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Follow the snowfall</p>
        <h3>24 hours. 48 hours. 7 days.</h3>
        <p>See forecast snowfall over the next 24 hours, 48 hours, and seven local days, then dig into hourly conditions to understand when it arrives.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Read the elevation</p>
        <h3>Base. Mid. Summit.</h3>
        <p>Explore forecast views from base to summit, with temperature and wind context. Elevation detail depends on the weather source.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pick your moment</p>
        <h3>Your Ski Signal.</h3>
        <p>Get a suggested riding window with the conditions behind it and a confidence level. Know what makes a day worth a closer look.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="weather-details">
      <article>
        <h3>Watch a storm take shape</h3>
        <p>Follow expected storm arrival, peak snowfall, and snowfall periods. Radar adds a view of recent precipitation around the mountain.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Make powder alerts your own</h3>
        <p>Choose your snowfall threshold, wind limit, and forecast confidence for favorite resorts. Set quiet hours and turn alerts on when you want them.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Look beyond the snow total</h3>
        <p>Explore snow-quality estimates, visibility, wind exposure, and freezing levels where available. A big number is only one part of the day ahead.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>See what backs the forecast</h3>
        <p>Check the weather sources, update times, and confidence behind the outlook, with mountain observations where available.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <a href="/weather/" class="btn" data-track-cta="homepage-weather-details">Explore the weather features &rarr;</a>
    <p class="feature-note">A preview of the app we&rsquo;re building. Forecast detail and observations vary by mountain and data availability.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- What it does -->
<section class="band" id="about">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">What it does</p>
    <h2>One app for the whole mountain day</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      SkiBuds started on the chairlifts in Whistler, from conversations about what riders
      actually wanted on the mountain. The rebuild connects that community with the tools
      to plan a day, explore a resort, and remember every run.
    </p>

    <div class="origin-gallery" aria-label="The SkiBuds community on the mountain">
      <figure>
        {% image "/_includes/images/skibuds-riders-flag.jpg", "SkiBuds riders gathered on a snowy mountain, holding their blue SkiBuds flag", "(min-width: 641px) 65vw, 100vw", "origin-gallery__image", "lazy", "auto", [640, 1080] %}
        <figcaption>Good days are better together.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        {% image "/_includes/images/skibuds-crew-flag.jpg", "Two SkiBuds riders holding their flag beneath a glacier", "(min-width: 641px) 35vw, 100vw", "origin-gallery__image", "lazy", "auto", [640, 1080] %}
        <figcaption>From our crew to yours.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2" />
          <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4" />
          <path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87" />
          <path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75" />
        </svg>
        <h3>Ride with people at your level</h3>
        <p>Discover skiers and snowboarders by ability, riding style, and availability. Check out profiles, send a friend request, and find people looking for your kind of day.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M21 11.5a8.4 8.4 0 0 1-.9 3.8 8.5 8.5 0 0 1-7.6 4.7 8.4 8.4 0 0 1-3.8-.9L3 21l1.9-5.7a8.4 8.4 0 0 1-.9-3.8 8.5 8.5 0 0 1 4.7-7.6 8.4 8.4 0 0 1 3.8-.9h.5a8.5 8.5 0 0 1 8 8Z" />
        </svg>
        <h3>Keep your group together</h3>
        <p>Go from mountain and city chats to private conversations and group messages. Share photos, make a plan, and use opt-in friend locations on the map to help regroup.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M3 20 10 5l4 8 2-3 5 10Z" />
          <circle cx="12" cy="3.6" r="1.6" />
        </svg>
        <h3>Track your runs</h3>
        <p>Record your day with GPS and automatic run and lift detection. Follow run count, vertical, distance, and speed, then revisit your route and activity history.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="m3 5 6-2 6 2 6-2v16l-6 2-6-2-6 2ZM9 3v16M15 5v16" />
        </svg>
        <h3>Get to know the mountain</h3>
        <p>Explore available trail and lift maps, switch terrain views, and find your position on the mountain. Download supported resort base maps before heading out of service.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="3" /><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="1.5" /><path d="m3 17 6-6 4 4 3-3 5 5" />
        </svg>
        <h3>Share the good parts</h3>
        <p>Post photo stories from the mountain and turn a tracked session into a Day Recap. Send your stats to a chat or story while keeping the exact route private.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="m12 3 2.8 5.7 6.3.9-4.6 4.5 1.1 6.3L12 17.4l-5.6 3 1.1-6.3L3 9.6l6.2-.9Z" />
        </svg>
        <h3>Keep your mountains close</h3>
        <p>Save favorite resorts and open each mountain&rsquo;s conditions, maps, and conversations from the same place. Add community lift and trail reports while you&rsquo;re there.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Ability levels -->
<section class="band band--tint" id="levels">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Ride at your level</p>
    <h2>Find your pace. Pick your terrain.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Share your ability and riding style, then use discovery filters to find people
      who want a similar pace and terrain. Start the conversation before the first chair.
    </p>

    <div class="levels">
      <div class="level">
        <span class="level__mark mark-green" aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span>
        <span class="level__name">Beginner</span>
        <span class="level__note">Learning the mountain. Groomers, easy terrain, no pressure.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="level">
        <span class="level__mark mark-blue" aria-hidden="true">&#9632;</span>
        <span class="level__name">Intermediate</span>
        <span class="level__note">Comfortable most places. Happy to lap groomers all day.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="level">
        <span class="level__mark mark-black" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;</span>
        <span class="level__name">Advanced</span>
        <span class="level__note">Steeps, bumps, and trees. Looking for people who keep up.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="level">
        <span class="level__mark mark-black" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;&#9670;</span>
        <span class="level__name">Expert</span>
        <span class="level__note">Technical terrain and challenging lines. Find riders with a similar approach.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="feature-note">Discovery also includes Semi-Advanced, Backcountry, and Park options,
      with riding-style filters for groomers, powder, moguls, trees, and more.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="day-plan" aria-labelledby="day-plan-heading">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">From the first forecast to the last run</p>
    <h2 id="day-plan-heading">Turn a promising forecast into a day together</h2>
    <ol class="day-flow">
      <li><h3>Check the outlook</h3><p>Open the forecast for your favorite mountains, look at the week ahead, and find a riding window that works for you.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Bring your crew</h3><p>Find riders, open a group conversation, and agree on a mountain and a meeting point.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Ride and remember it</h3><p>Use the map, track your runs, and share a Day Recap when you&rsquo;re back at the base.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <a href="#waitlist" class="btn" data-track-cta="product-join-waitlist">Join the launch waitlist &rarr;</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band launch-band" id="status" aria-labelledby="launch-heading">
  <div class="shell launch-panel">
    <div class="launch-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">SkiBuds launch · {{ site.app.launchYear }}</p>
      <h2 id="launch-heading">Get the first chair on launch day.</h2>
      <p class="lede">We&rsquo;re rebuilding SkiBuds for iOS and Android. Join riders following along, and we&rsquo;ll let you know when the new app is ready.</p>
      <div class="launch-count"><strong>{{ site.waitlist.count | comma }}</strong><span>riders on the waitlist</span></div>
      <a class="launch-social" href="{{ site.social.instagram }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track-cta="instagram-launch-updates">Follow <strong>@skibudsapp</strong> for build updates &rarr;</a>
    </div>
    <div class="launch-signup">
      <div class="board" aria-label="App launch status">
        <div class="board__head"><span>Availability</span><span>{{ site.app.launchYear }}</span></div>
        <div class="board__row"><span class="board__label">iOS</span><span class="board__state"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ site.app.iosStatus }}</span></div>
        <div class="board__row"><span class="board__label">Android</span><span class="board__state"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ site.app.androidStatus }}</span></div>
      </div>
      <form id="waitlist" class="waitlist-form" action="https://api.buttondown.email/v1/subscribers" method="POST" novalidate>
        <input type="hidden" name="tags" value="ski-buds-waitlist">
        <label for="email-input">Your email</label>
        <div class="waitlist-form__controls">
          <input type="email" id="email-input" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required autocomplete="email" aria-describedby="email-hint">
          <button type="submit" class="btn">Join the waitlist</button>
        </div>
        <span id="email-hint" class="visually-hidden">Enter your email address to get SkiBuds launch updates.</span>
        <p class="form-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Partners -->
<section class="band band--tint">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Partners</p>
    <h2>Good people we ride with</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      SkiBuds works with shops, clubs, and trip organizers across North America.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
      <a href="/affiliates" class="btn btn--quiet">See all partners &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
